<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That was pretty nerve-wracking, huh?”</span> He laughs, pulling his shirt off as he walks over to his normal clothes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“There were so many people! But I think we did pretty good, haha. Mind turning around while I get changed? I mean, I know you’ve seen it all before, but it’s still a little embarrassing.”</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">You just stand there, staring at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> silently for a moment before asking if he’s okay.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Okay? Yeah, why wouldn’t I be?”</span> He smiles, pulling his shirt on and laughing at your silly question, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I just got this really cool award and dad said we were going to have a pizza party after to celebrate! Oh, yeah, I meant to ask you if you wanted to come over for it? I think you’ve earned some pizza too! Plus, we can watch a movie or something and”</span> You continue to stare at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, he seems completely normal and unphased, but you can’t get that brief second on stage where you say his expression faulter out of your mind. <br>
<br>
<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>?”</span> There is a knock at the door. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly pulls up his shorts before yelling for them to come in. His father and brother enter the room, <span style="Color: Yellow"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> looking more than a little upset.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You were great out there, bud! I’m so proud of you!”</span> His dad walks over and hugs <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, who giggles and thanks him. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And I’m really sorry about-! I really thought-!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad sighs, not knowing what to say, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m just… sorry.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s alright.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I know it can all be a bit weird sometimes. It’s a pretty cool award though, right? Look, my name is all shiny and stuff! Oh, what did you think of my little speech? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> and I may have stayed up a little last night working on it, but I think it was nice. Short and sweet.”</span> He smiles proudly, looking to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> <span style="Color: Pink">whose frown instantly becomes a smile as he pats his little brother on the head.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I think you nailed it.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You looked great up there. I’d be jealous, but I think your new coolness is going to rub off on me.”</span> They both laugh before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> turns to you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks for being up there with him. That stuff you said was really nice. I’m glad <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> has someone like you to support him. It’s important to be there for people you care about.”</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">That last part was very clearly not directed at you.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, that’s not fair. You know”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad starts to explain, but he is quickly cut off. <br>
